    Then ${e_k | k in ZZ^d}$ is an orthonormal basis of $L^2 (pi^d).$
    For $w = (w_k)_(k in ZZ^d)$ with $w_k >= 0$ define $ F(z) = sum_(k in ZZ^d) w_k z^k.$
    We see $ sum_(n=0)^N sum_(m=0)^N c_n overline(c)_m F(z_n dot z_m^(-1)) >= 0 $
    for $N in NN, c_1,...,c_N in CC, z_1,...,z_N in pi^d.$
    Now $Phi(z) = (Phi_k (z))_(k in ZZ^d), med Phi_k (z) = w_k^(1/2) z^k.$ 
    This defines a feature map $Phi: pi^d ->  cal(l)^2 (NN_0^d)$ s.t. $K(z,xi) <= chevron.l Phi(z), Phi(xi) chevron.r_(cal(l)^2 (NN_0^d)).$
    In harmonic analysis it is shown that $aa = "span"{Phi_k | k in ZZ^d}$ (space of trigonometric polynomials) is dense in $C(pi^d).$
