Apply @thm:mercer to RKHS theory. $ K in C(X' times X')$ positive definite.
The operator $T_K = S^*_K S_K$ has kernel $K$ (recall $S^*_K$ is the embedding operator).
Thus $T_K$ satisfies all conditions of @thm:mercer.
$ K(x,y) = sum_(j=1)^(oo) lambda_j phi_j (x) overline(phi_j) (y) $
converges uniformly and absolutely.
Now let $ H = {sum_(j=1)^(oo) a_j sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j | (a_j)_(j=1)^oo in cal(l)^2 (NN) }, $
and define an inner product on $H$: For $f, g in H$,
$ f = sum_(j=1)^(oo) a_j sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j, quad g = sum_(j=1)^(oo) b_j sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j, $
the inner product is
$ chevron.l f,g chevron.r_H = sum_(j=1)^(oo) a_j overline(b_j). $

Note that
$ |sum_(j=1)^(oo) a_j sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j (x) | <= underbrace((sum_(j=1)^(oo) |a_j|)^(1/2), ||(a_j)||_(cal(l)^2)) underbrace((sum_(j=1)^(oo) lambda_j |phi_j (x)|^2)^(1/2), "bounded by Th. 4.23") $
i.e. all objects are well-defined.

