#proposition[
  Let $(X', d)$ a compact metric space, $mu$ a finite Borel measeure, $"supp"(mu) = X'$, $K in C(X' times X')$ is positive definite.
  Further, let ${phi_j | j in NN}, {lambda_j | j in NN}$defined by $T_K phi_j = lambda_j phi_j, j in NN.$
  Then
  + $H = hh_K$,
  + $T_K^(1/2): ker(T_K)^perp --> H$ is an isometric isomorphism.
]

#proof[
  + For $x in X'$ we have (from @thm:mercer) $ K(x, dot) = sum_(j=1)^(oo) sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j (x) sqrt(lambda_j) overline(phi_j). $
    Recall $ sum_(j=1)^(oo) |sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j (x)|^2 = sum_(j=1)^(oo) lambda_j |phi_j (x)|^2 < oo. $
    Let $ f = sum_(j=1)^(oo) a_j sqrt(lambda_j) phi_j, (a_j)_(j=1)^oo subset cal(l)^2 (NN), x in X'. $
    Then $chevron.l f, K(x, dot) chevron.r_H = ... = f(x). $
    Hence $K$ is the reproducing kernel for $H$, thus $H = hh_K.$
  + Since  $lambda_j > 0, j in NN$, we have $ T_K^(1/2) = sum_(j=1)^(oo) lambda_j^(1/2) chevron.l dot, phi_j chevron.r_(L^2 (mu)) phi_j. $
    Let $f in ker(T_K^(1/2))^perp$, then $(chevron.l f, phi_j chevron.r)_(j=1)^oo in cal(l)^2 (NN).$
    Thus $T_K^(1/2) in H$.
    Moreover, $ ||T_K^(1/2) f||_H^2 = sum_(j=1)^(oo) |chevron.l f,phi_j chevron.r|^2 = ||f||^2_(L^2(mu)). $
    Hence $T_K^(1/2)$ is an isometry.
    ...
    Take $(a_j)_j$ and define $g = sum_(j=1)^(oo) a_j phi_j in ker(T_K)^perp.$
    Apply $T_K^(1/2)$ to $g$:
    $ |T_K^(1/2) g(x)| <= ||(a_j)_j||_(cal(l)^2 (NN)) underbrace((sum_(j=1)^(oo) lambda_j |phi_j (x)|^2)^(1/2), "converges pointwise") $
]


