#remark[
  Assume one of (i)-(iii) from @cor:5.17.
  Then, assuming $L$ satisfies the conditions in @cor:5.17, we have $A(lambda) <= lambda||f^*_(L,P,hh_K)||^2_hh_K$ and $ ||f^*_lambda - f^*_(L,P,hh_K)||_hh_K -->_(lambda->0_+) 0. $
  For $lambda > 0$, $f^*_lambda$ is a minimizer of $rr_(L,P,lambda)$, since
  $ lambda ||f^*_lambda||^2_hh_K <= rr_(L,P) (f) + lambda||f||^2_hh_K - rr^*_(L,P,hh_K) $ 
  for every $f in hh_K.$
  Then $lambda ||f^*_lambda||^2_hh_K <= A(lambda) <= rr_(L,P)(0) - rr^*_(L,P,hh_K).$
  Hence, $A(dot)$ is a bounded function of $lambda$ and $ ||f^*_lambda||^2_hh_K <= (A(lambda))/lambda -->_(lambda->oo) oo. $
  Hence $lim_(lambda->oo) f^*_lambda = f^*_oo = 0.$
