== Dependence of the Minimizer on the Measure.
#theorem[
  Let $p,p' in [1,oo)$ s.t. $1/p + 1/p' = 1$, $P$ a probability measure on $X' times Y$, $L$ a convex $P$-integrable Nemitski loss function of order $p$, $hh_K$ a RKHS with $K$ measurable and bounded.
  Then for every $lambda > 0$ there is $h in cal(L)^p' (X' times Y, P)$ with
  1. $h(x,y) in partial L(x,y,f^*_lambda (x))$ for $(x,y) in X' times Y,$
  2. $f^*_lambda = -1/(2 lambda) integral_(X' times Y) h(x,y) K(dot,y) dif P(x,y) =: cal(K)_p h,$
  3. $h in cal(L)^1 (X' times Y, P),$
  4. $||f^*_(P,lambda) - f^*_(tilde(P),lambda)||_hh_K <= 1/lambda ||kk_p h - kk_tilde(P) h||_hh_K$ for every probability measure $tilde(P)$ for which $L$ is a $tilde(P)$-integrable Nemitski loss function.
]<thm:5.19>

#note[
  - $L^p (X', mu)$ contains equivalence classes of functions.
  - $ll^p (X', mu)$ contains the functions themselves.
]

#proof[
  (i) and (ii) follow from Thm 5.13.\
  (iii) using reproducing property to get
  $ ||f^*_(P,lambda)||_oo <= ||K||_oo ||f^*_(P,lambda)||_hh_K <= ||K||_oo ((rr_(L,P)(0))/lambda)^(1/2) =: B_lambda < oo. $
  $L$ is $tilde(P)$ integrable Nemitski loss function.
  Hence there is $tilde(b) in ll^1 (tilde(P))$, and increasing $tilde(h): [0,oo) -> [0,oo)$ s.t.
  $ L(x,y,t) <= tilde(b)(x,y) + tilde(h)(|t|) quad forall (x,y,t) in X' times Y times RR. $
  Use (i) and Prop 5.10 to get
  $ |h(x,y) <= sup|partial L(x,y,f^*_(P,lambda)(x)| <= |L(x,y,dot)|_([-1+||f^*_(P,lambda)||_oo, 1+||f^*_(P,lambda)||_oo]). $
  This gives
  $ |h(x,y)| &<= |L(x,y,dot)|_([-1+B_lambda,1+B_lambda]) <=^((*)) 1/(1+B_lambda) ||L(x,y,dot)|_([-2+2B_lambda,2+2B_lambda])||_oo \
             &<= (tilde(b)(x,y) + tilde(h)(2+2B_lambda))/(1+B_lambda) $
  #box(width: 100%, stroke: 0.5pt, outset: 5pt)[
    (\*): For every convex function $phi: RR -> RR$ which is locally Lipschitz continuous on $[-t,t]$, we have
    $ |phi|_([-t,t]) |_1 <= 2/t ||phi_([-2t,2t])||_oo. $
  ]
  Hence $h in ll^1 (X' times Y, tilde(P)).$\
  (iv) By definition of the subdifferential
  $ h(x,y) [f^*_(tilde(P),lambda)(x) - f^*_(P,lambda)(x)] <= L(x,y,f^*_(tilde(P),lambda)(x) - L(x,y,f^*_(P,lambda)(x). $
  Integrating w.r.t. $tilde(P)$, we get
  $ integral_(X' times Y) h(x,y) [f^*_(tilde(P),lambda)(x) - f^*_(P,lambda)(x)] dif tilde(P)(x,y) <= rr_(L,tilde(P))(f^*_(tilde(P),lambda)) - rr_(L,tilde(P))(f^*_(P,lambda)) <= 0. $
  Moreover,
  $ integral_(X' times Y) h(x,y) [...] dif tilde(P)(x,y) &= integral_(X' times Y) h(x,y) chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda), K(dot,y) chevron.r_hh_K dif tilde(P)(x,y) \
   &= chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda),  integral_(X' times Y) h(x,y) K(dot, y) dif P(x,y) chevron.r_hh_K \
   &= chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda) , kk_tilde(P) h chevron.r_hh_K $
  Further,
  $ chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda), kk_tilde(P) h - kk_P h chevron.r_hh_K <= ||f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda)||hh_K dot ||kk_tilde(P) h - kk_P h||_hh_K. $

  Claim: $ chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda), kk_tilde(P) h - kk_P h chevron.r_hh_K >= lambda ||f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda)||_hh_K (**)$
  $ 2lambda chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda), f^*_(P,lambda) chevron.r_hh_K + lambda ||f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda)||^2_hh_K = lambda||f^*_(tilde(P),lambda)||^2_hh_K - 2||f^*_(P,lambda)||^2_hh_K. $
  Therefore,
  $ chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda), kk_tilde(P) h + 2 lambda f^*_(P,lambda) chevron.r_hh_K + lambda ||f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda)||^2_hh_K = rr_(L,tilde(P),lambda)(f^*_(tilde(P)_lambda - rr_(L,tilde(P),lambda)(f^*_(P,lambda) <= 0. $
  We also have $ f^*_(P,lambda) = -1/(2lambda) kk_P h "("arrow.squiggly"representer theorem)". $
  $ chevron.l f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda), kk_tilde(P) h - kk_P h chevron.r_hh_K >= lambda ||f^*_(tilde(P),lambda) - f^*_(P,lambda)||^2_hh_K. $ 
  With this the statement follows.
]

